      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#onboarding"
      ],
      "text": "**Review Osmantic ODS for onboarding ideas (captured 2026-07-17): [github.com/Osmantic/ODS](https://github.com/Osmantic/ODS) \u2014 \"Osmantic Deployment System\"; adjacent competitor; onboarding is their strength.**\n- [ ] NOT just a wizard: a full local-AI-server orchestrator bundling **Open WebUI** (same lineage as us) + llama-server + LiteLLM + n8n + Whisper + Kokoro + Qdrant + SearXNG + ComfyUI as Docker containers\n- [ ] Mine:\n- [ ] Single-command zero-prereq installers (bash + PowerShell) with GPU auto-detect \u2192 model selection\n- [ ] A **bootstrap \"first chat in <2 min\"** mode (vs. our wizard's up-front model downloads)\n- [ ] A management dashboard\n- [ ] **Plug-and-play service folders** that rhyme with Sprigs\u2122\n- [ ] Our edge stays the slim Rootstock\u2122 + zero-egress Sprig\u2122 runtime + marketplace\n- [ ] Feeds the one-click-installer item above\n\n`#onboarding`\n`TODO.md:L899`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 600
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 910,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Concrete driver: the Docling *standard* sprig is ~5GB (docling-serve hard-pulls `docling-jobkit[ray,rq,vlm]` \u2192 ray/codeflare/kubernetes)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 911,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A sidecar variant (operator runs docling-serve, the sprig just sets `DOCLING_SERVER_URL` from a settings field) is the pragmatic path"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 912,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Offer BOTH standard (in-container, zero-egress) + sidecar for tika/docling"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 913,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "This is the spec's currently-unimplemented `delivery: service-endpoint` shape"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 914,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Work:"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 915,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(a) per-sprig settings schema + Admin UI field + persistence + dispatch read"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 916,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(b) service-endpoint/sidecar delivery that skips the pull and points capability config at the URL (sidecar \"graft\" = \"save URL\")"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 917,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(c) standard + sidecar catalog entries"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "431939fcd537ce56",
      "line_num": 909,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bonsai"
      ],
      "text": "**Configurable sprigs + sidecar-sprig variant (captured 2026-07-18): sprigs carry SETTINGS (per-entry schema \u2014 e.g. a service `url`) plus a sidecar sprig kind that points at an operator-run external service instead of shipping an artifact.**\n- [ ] Concrete driver: the Docling *standard* sprig is ~5GB (docling-serve hard-pulls `docling-jobkit[ray,rq,vlm]` \u2192 ray/codeflare/kubernetes)\n- [ ] A sidecar variant (operator runs docling-serve, the sprig just sets `DOCLING_SERVER_URL` from a settings field) is the pragmatic path\n- [ ] Offer BOTH standard (in-container, zero-egress) + sidecar for tika/docling\n- [ ] This is the spec's currently-unimplemented `delivery: service-endpoint` shape\n- [ ] Work:\n- [ ] (a) per-sprig settings schema + Admin UI field + persistence + dispatch read\n- [ ] (b) service-endpoint/sidecar delivery that skips the pull and points capability config at the URL (sidecar \"graft\" = \"save URL\")\n- [ ] (c) standard + sidecar catalog entries\n\n`#bonsai`\n`TODO.md:L909`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 690
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 920,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The cost doubles in `release_smoke` (native + amd64 builds) and the amd64 side pays QEMU tax on top"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 921,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Levers, roughly in order of payoff:"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 922,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(1) the frontend build output is arch-neutral JS/CSS/wasm \u2014 build it ONCE and COPY the same `build/` into both arch images instead of re-running Vite under emulation"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 923,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(2) buildx cache mounts for `node_modules` + `.svelte-kit` + Vite's cache dir so unchanged frontends skip the work"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 924,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(3) Dockerfile layer ordering so backend-only changes never bust the frontend layer"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 925,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Sourcemaps are already off in production builds (6c393d9)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 926,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**NOTE:** vite specific solutions may exist or svelte upgrades"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "609abdd5d97b89c7",
      "line_num": 919,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#perf"
      ],
      "text": "**Tighten the Vite build: it eats ~half the image build \u2014 full image build measured 3m37s with the Vite frontend stage taking roughly half (captured 2026-07-15 during the 3.0.0 release).**\n- [ ] The cost doubles in `release_smoke` (native + amd64 builds) and the amd64 side pays QEMU tax on top\n- [ ] Levers, roughly in order of payoff:\n- [ ] (1) the frontend build output is arch-neutral JS/CSS/wasm \u2014 build it ONCE and COPY the same `build/` into both arch images instead of re-running Vite under emulation\n- [ ] (2) buildx cache mounts for `node_modules` + `.svelte-kit` + Vite's cache dir so unchanged frontends skip the work\n- [ ] (3) Dockerfile layer ordering so backend-only changes never bust the frontend layer\n- [ ] Sourcemaps are already off in production builds (6c393d9)\n- [ ] **NOTE:** vite specific solutions may exist or svelte upgrades\n\n`#perf`\n`TODO.md:L919`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 780
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 929,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Knowledge-base population/reindex, image generation, model downloads, bulk transcription, and big uploads all run as synchronous requests or fire-and-forget threads"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 930,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Ad-hoc status today: `MODEL_DOWNLOAD_STATUS` dict, per-request `ThreadPoolExecutor` in audio.py"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 931,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Sequenced as unlock #4 (last) for the real-estate engagement 2026-07-30 \u2014 the November commitment needs no software; promote when a staged beat must become a real one"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 932,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Settle first: DB-backed in-process queue (single-container fit, Bonsai\u2122-friendly) vs redis-backed (already a dep) \u2014 lean DB-backed until multi-worker is real"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 933,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Build: job table (id/type/owner/state/progress/error) + bounded worker pool + one status endpoint (poll or SSE)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 934,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Surface running jobs in admin diagnostics and the requesting user's UI"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 935,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fold in prior art: the download-watchdog TODO (stalled-download detection) and the upload/download UX memories (progress bars, time estimates)"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "8c65aae7da62c46d",
      "line_num": 928,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Job queue for long-running processes (idea captured 2026-07-06): no unified queue, no retry, no concurrency caps, no visible progress. ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] Knowledge-base population/reindex, image generation, model downloads, bulk transcription, and big uploads all run as synchronous requests or fire-and-forget threads\n- [ ] Ad-hoc status today: `MODEL_DOWNLOAD_STATUS` dict, per-request `ThreadPoolExecutor` in audio.py\n- [ ] Sequenced as unlock #4 (last) for the real-estate engagement 2026-07-30 \u2014 the November commitment needs no software; promote when a staged beat must become a real one\n- [ ] Settle first: DB-backed in-process queue (single-container fit, Bonsai\u2122-friendly) vs redis-backed (already a dep) \u2014 lean DB-backed until multi-worker is real\n- [ ] Build: job table (id/type/owner/state/progress/error) + bounded worker pool + one status endpoint (poll or SSE)\n- [ ] Surface running jobs in admin diagnostics and the requesting user's UI\n- [ ] Fold in prior art: the download-watchdog TODO (stalled-download detection) and the upload/download UX memories (progress bars, time estimates)\n\n`TODO.md:L928`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 870
    },
    {
