    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 186,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY` is unset in `.env.example`, the `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yaml`, and `distribution.env`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 187,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`SecurityHeadersMiddleware` (`main.py:1473`, `utils/security_headers.py::set_security_headers()`) builds headers purely from env vars."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 188,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`routers/diagnostics.py:610` already grades the absence \"degraded\" \u2014 the system knows and cannot stop anything."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 189,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Stakes rose twice this month: the marketplace renders third-party listings, and community.sage.is opens in weeks."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 190,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Ship a `scripts/gates/` check on the `startr-swap/check.py` `--check`/`--self-test` shape, asserting `distribution.env` sets a policy."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 191,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Gate on `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`, NOT enforcement \u2014 gating on enforcement pressures somebody into shipping an untested policy, and this app has never run one."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 192,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Sequence: report-only first, collect violations from a real session, then enforce."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 193,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Exceptions the policy must carry: `https://startr.style/style.css` in both frontends (`app/src/app.html:31`, `pages/shell.py:206`), Artifacts `srcdoc` frames, Pyodide, the WASM sprigs, every inline style."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 194,
          "tags": [
            "#security"
          ],
          "text": "**Write and ship the policy itself; omit `unsafe-eval` on purpose** (Switch 2 of the 2026-08-15 poka-yoke resolution; \"not a today thing\"). The gate proves a policy is set; this is the policy."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 195,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Omitting `unsafe-eval` makes `new Function(...)` throw \u2014 closes the browser half of the `execute` door with one directive."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 196,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Keep `'unsafe-inline'` for now: the branding panel, `pages/assets/*.js`, `sprigs/ui_dispatch.py`, and `SetupDialog.svelte` depend on inline handlers; nonce-based CSP is its own later job."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 197,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Acceptance test already wired: `routers/diagnostics.py` flips `csp_missing` off on a stock deploy."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 198,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Report-only first, per the parent."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "3e9b273cd57a46ec",
      "line_num": 185,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**CSP-configured gate: assert a CSP is set \u2014 an unset header and a deliberate omission look identical to the process (charted 2026-08-15 in the poka-yoke pass). #security #critical ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] `CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY` is unset in `.env.example`, the `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yaml`, and `distribution.env`.\n- [ ] `SecurityHeadersMiddleware` (`main.py:1473`, `utils/security_headers.py::set_security_headers()`) builds headers purely from env vars.\n- [ ] `routers/diagnostics.py:610` already grades the absence \"degraded\" \u2014 the system knows and cannot stop anything.\n- [ ] Stakes rose twice this month: the marketplace renders third-party listings, and community.sage.is opens in weeks.\n- [ ] Ship a `scripts/gates/` check on the `startr-swap/check.py` `--check`/`--self-test` shape, asserting `distribution.env` sets a policy.\n- [ ] Gate on `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`, NOT enforcement \u2014 gating on enforcement pressures somebody into shipping an untested policy, and this app has never run one.\n- [ ] Sequence: report-only first, collect violations from a real session, then enforce.\n- [ ] Exceptions the policy must carry: `https://startr.style/style.css` in both frontends (`app/src/app.html:31`, `pages/shell.py:206`), Artifacts `srcdoc` frames, Pyodide, the WASM sprigs, every inline style.\n- [ ] **Write and ship the policy itself; omit `unsafe-eval` on purpose** (Switch 2 of the 2026-08-15 poka-yoke resolution; \"not a today thing\"). The gate proves a policy is set; this is the policy. #security\n- [ ] Omitting `unsafe-eval` makes `new Function(...)` throw \u2014 closes the browser half of the `execute` door with one directive.\n- [ ] Keep `'unsafe-inline'` for now: the branding panel, `pages/assets/*.js`, `sprigs/ui_dispatch.py`, and `SetupDialog.svelte` depend on inline handlers; nonce-based CSP is its own later job.\n- [ ] Acceptance test already wired: `routers/diagnostics.py` flips `csp_missing` off on a stock deploy.\n- [ ] Report-only first, per the parent.\n\n`TODO.md:L185`",
