        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "e5c8468b622646c1",
      "line_num": 223,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Coordinated langchain major bump: bump the langchain/langchain-community/langchain-core trio (rag-loaders Sprig\u2122 side) past 0.3.x to drop the `CVE-2026-34070` suppression.**\n- [ ] `.trivyignore` suppresses `CVE-2026-34070`: path traversal in `langchain_core`'s legacy `load_prompt()`, unreachable in this codebase \u2014 see `.trivyignore` comment.\n- [ ] The fix (`langchain-core==1.2.22`) needs `langchain-core<1.0.0` dropped, which both pinned sprig-side packages require (`langchain==0.3.30`, `langchain-community==0.3.27`, `app/backend/requirements.txt:51-56`).\n- [ ] Plan and test the coordinated bump, then remove the `.trivyignore` entry.\n\n`TODO.md:L223`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2670
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 233,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The only graceful path today is `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` \u2014 silent email-match linking, useless when the local email differs from the provider's."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 234,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Also an account-takeover footgun if email control is weaker than account control."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 235,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Scope: build Patterns A + B, lift the one-provider-per-user schema limit, harden the admin controls with Poka-Yoke devices."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 236,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Schema lift to multi-provider stacking**: migration ships before any UX work."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 237,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Replace single `oauth_sub TEXT UNIQUE` with per-provider `UNIQUE` columns `google_sub`, `github_sub`, `microsoft_sub` (+ `apple_sub` when Apple lands)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 238,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Generic `oidc` keeps `oauth_sub` as catch-all."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 239,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Rewrite every `user.oauth_sub` callsite to `Users.get_user_by_oauth_sub(provider, sub)`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 240,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Pattern A \u2014 Settings-driven link/unlink**: Account Settings \u2192 \"Connected providers\" lists each linked provider with an unlink button, plus Connect buttons for the rest."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 241,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "OAuth round-trip carries a session-bound `state` token; callback attaches `<provider>_sub` to the already-signed-in user."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 242,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Pattern B \u2014 OAuth-first claim flow with magic-link verify**: no oauth_sub or email match \u2192 redirect to `/auth/claim?provider=google&sub=...&temp=<token>` instead of 403 or auto-create."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 243,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "User enters their AI-UI email; the magic link attaches the identity."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 244,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "No-existing-account branch goes to a separate create flow gated on `ENABLE_OAUTH_SIGNUP` + allowlist policy."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 245,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Per-provider link mode** (replaces global `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`): each provider gets `<provider>_link_mode`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 246,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Modes: `silent_merge_by_email` (current behavior), `verify_via_magic_link` (Pattern B pipeline), `disabled` (Pattern A only)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 247,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fresh-install default: `verify_via_magic_link` if SMTP is configured, else `silent_merge_by_email` with a save-time warning."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 248,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Migration: `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL=True` \u2192 all providers `silent_merge_by_email`; `=False` \u2192 `disabled`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 249,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Global toggle stays as fallback one major version, then drops."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 250,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Replace raw 403 with a real status page**: redirect `handle_callback` failures to `/auth/status?reason=<signup_disabled|allowlist_blocked|domain_blocked|role_pending|email_taken>&email=<masked>`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 251,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Replaces `HTTPException(403, ACCESS_PROHIBITED)` at [utils/oauth.py:508-511](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/oauth.py#L508); API surface keeps the 403 for programmatic clients."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 252,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Frontend route renders branded copy + \"request approval\" CTA (mailto or webhook)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 256,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Per-provider allowed-domains policy** (replaces global `OAUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAINS`): each provider block gets `<provider>_allowed_domains`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 257,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Example: Google `@openco.ca` only while GitHub stays open, Microsoft `@school.edu, @school.k12.org`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 258,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Provider blocks already exist at [config.py:316-700](app/backend/sage_is_ai/config.py#L316); extend with the domain field."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 259,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Per-user OAuth allowlist**: `oauth_eligible BOOLEAN DEFAULT True` on the user record plus per-provider overrides (`google_allowed`, etc.)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 260,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Lets a workshop lock to the invited cohort even when the domain allowlist matches."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 261,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Default is eligible; restrictive mode is one toggle."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 262,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Save-time Poka-Yoke on admin OAuth config**:"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 263,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Refuse to save `ENABLE_OAUTH_SIGNUP=True` with empty/wildcard allowed-domains without an explicit \"I understand this is open registration\" confirmation toggle."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 264,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Treat an empty allowed-domains list as \"no one\" (fail-closed), not \"everyone\" (fail-open)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 265,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Block enabling Pattern B when SMTP isn't configured \u2014 the magic link would never arrive. Inline error: \"Configure email first (Settings \u2192 Email).\""
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 266,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Inline preview after each field change: \"With current settings, the following can sign up: Google @openco.ca only; GitHub open to allowlisted users only.\""
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 267,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**\"Simulate sign-in\" admin diagnostic** \u2014 highest-leverage Poka-Yoke: admin pastes an email + picks a provider; system shows the end-to-end outcome with no DB changes."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 268,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Outcomes: \"Would link to existing user X\" / \"Would create new pending user\" / \"Would 403 \u2014 not in domain allowlist\" / \"Would 403 \u2014 user not on per-user allowlist\"."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 269,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Catches misconfiguration before a real user hits it."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 270,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**i18n** all new user-facing copy (status pages, claim flow, settings labels)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 271,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Audit log** entry on every link/unlink event: `(timestamp, user_id, provider, sub, action, actor)` \u2014 admin or user."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 272,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Migration safety**: migration populates the typed columns from existing `oauth_sub = \"google@...\"`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 273,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Old field stays nullable one release for rollback, removed in N+1."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "dea207944cfe6789",
      "line_num": 232,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**OAuth identity linking v1: let users attach Google/GitHub/Microsoft to existing accounts whose email doesn't match the provider's email; decisions confirmed in plan thread 2026-05-28 ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md)).**\n- [ ] The only graceful path today is `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL` \u2014 silent email-match linking, useless when the local email differs from the provider's.\n- [ ] Also an account-takeover footgun if email control is weaker than account control.\n- [ ] Scope: build Patterns A + B, lift the one-provider-per-user schema limit, harden the admin controls with Poka-Yoke devices.\n- [ ] **Schema lift to multi-provider stacking**: migration ships before any UX work.\n- [ ] Replace single `oauth_sub TEXT UNIQUE` with per-provider `UNIQUE` columns `google_sub`, `github_sub`, `microsoft_sub` (+ `apple_sub` when Apple lands).\n- [ ] Generic `oidc` keeps `oauth_sub` as catch-all.\n- [ ] Rewrite every `user.oauth_sub` callsite to `Users.get_user_by_oauth_sub(provider, sub)`.\n- [ ] **Pattern A \u2014 Settings-driven link/unlink**: Account Settings \u2192 \"Connected providers\" lists each linked provider with an unlink button, plus Connect buttons for the rest.\n- [ ] OAuth round-trip carries a session-bound `state` token; callback attaches `<provider>_sub` to the already-signed-in user.\n- [ ] **Pattern B \u2014 OAuth-first claim flow with magic-link verify**: no oauth_sub or email match \u2192 redirect to `/auth/claim?provider=google&sub=...&temp=<token>` instead of 403 or auto-create.\n- [ ] User enters their AI-UI email; the magic link attaches the identity.\n- [ ] No-existing-account branch goes to a separate create flow gated on `ENABLE_OAUTH_SIGNUP` + allowlist policy.\n- [ ] **Per-provider link mode** (replaces global `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL`): each provider gets `<provider>_link_mode`.\n- [ ] Modes: `silent_merge_by_email` (current behavior), `verify_via_magic_link` (Pattern B pipeline), `disabled` (Pattern A only).\n- [ ] Fresh-install default: `verify_via_magic_link` if SMTP is configured, else `silent_merge_by_email` with a save-time warning.\n- [ ] Migration: `OAUTH_MERGE_ACCOUNTS_BY_EMAIL=True` \u2192 all providers `silent_merge_by_email`; `=False` \u2192 `disabled`.\n- [ ] Global toggle stays as fallback one major version, then drops.\n- [ ] **Replace raw 403 with a real status page**: redirect `handle_callback` failures to `/auth/status?reason=<signup_disabled|allowlist_blocked|domain_blocked|role_pending|email_taken>&email=<masked>`.\n- [ ] Replaces `HTTPException(403, ACCESS_PROHIBITED)` at [utils/oauth.py:508-511](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/oauth.py#L508); API surface keeps the 403 for programmatic clients.\n- [ ] Frontend route renders branded copy + \"request approval\" CTA (mailto or webhook).\n- [ ] **Per-provider allowed-domains policy** (replaces global `OAUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAINS`): each provider block gets `<provider>_allowed_domains`.\n- [ ] Example: Google `@openco.ca` only while GitHub stays open, Microsoft `@school.edu, @school.k12.org`.\n- [ ] Provider blocks already exist at [config.py:316-700](app/backend/sage_is_ai/config.py#L316); extend with the domain field.\n- [ ] **Per-user OAuth allowlist**: `oauth_eligible BOOLEAN DEFAULT True` on the user record plus per-provider overrides (`google_allowed`, etc.).\n- [ ] Lets a workshop lock to the invited cohort even when the domain allowlist matches.\n- [ ] Default is eligible; restrictive mode is one toggle.\n- [ ] **Save-time Poka-Yoke on admin OAuth config**:\n- [ ] Refuse to save `ENABLE_OAUTH_SIGNUP=True` with empty/wildcard allowed-domains without an explicit \"I understand this is open registration\" confirmation toggle.\n- [ ] Treat an empty allowed-domains list as \"no one\" (fail-closed), not \"everyone\" (fail-open).\n- [ ] Block enabling Pattern B when SMTP isn't configured \u2014 the magic link would never arrive. Inline error: \"Configure email first (Settings \u2192 Email).\"\n- [ ] Inline preview after each field change: \"With current settings, the following can sign up: Google @openco.ca only; GitHub open to allowlisted users only.\"\n- [ ] **\"Simulate sign-in\" admin diagnostic** \u2014 highest-leverage Poka-Yoke: admin pastes an email + picks a provider; system shows the end-to-end outcome with no DB changes.\n- [ ] Outcomes: \"Would link to existing user X\" / \"Would create new pending user\" / \"Would 403 \u2014 not in domain allowlist\" / \"Would 403 \u2014 user not on per-user allowlist\".\n- [ ] Catches misconfiguration before a real user hits it.\n- [ ] **i18n** all new user-facing copy (status pages, claim flow, settings labels).\n- [ ] **Audit log** entry on every link/unlink event: `(timestamp, user_id, provider, sub, action, actor)` \u2014 admin or user.\n- [ ] **Migration safety**: migration populates the typed columns from existing `oauth_sub = \"google@...\"`.\n- [ ] Old field stays nullable one release for rollback, removed in N+1.\n\n`TODO.md:L232`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2760
