          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 738,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Per-user landing-page preference (chat vs home vs a chosen Space vs part of Notes): needs persistence + a settings screen; changes what `/` means for a signed-in reader"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 739,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Do not hardcode the option list \u2014 Notes may be replaced by Silverbullet; read the choices from what the instance has"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "d78e6316f0a7a385",
      "line_num": 735,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#frontend",
        "#ux"
      ],
      "text": "**Sidebar toggles for Home and Calendar, and a landing-page preference (Alexander, 2026-08-09): two features, one shared settings surface \u2014 neither gets tacked onto a page build. ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] Not blocked on the top nav: the dashboard surfaces now share a `DashboardShell` with one `LINKS` list and Calendar joined it (losing its \"Soon\" badge and `preventDefault` dead link) \u2014 the sidebar is this card\n- [ ] Per-surface show-in-sidebar toggles, mirroring Spaces. `Sidebar.svelte` hardcodes `/home`, `/notes`, `/workshop` \u2014 a change of shape, not a fourth `<a>`\n- [ ] Per-user landing-page preference (chat vs home vs a chosen Space vs part of Notes): needs persistence + a settings screen; changes what `/` means for a signed-in reader\n- [ ] Do not hardcode the option list \u2014 Notes may be replaced by Silverbullet; read the choices from what the instance has\n\n`#frontend` `#ux`\n`TODO.md:L735`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 6090
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 741,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/admin/sprigs` vs `/pages/admin/sprigs` and `/admin/diagnostics` vs `/pages/admin/diagnostics` are both live \u2014 same data, same deployment \u2014 so judging is the cheapest it will ever be"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 742,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A green suite is the WEAKEST evidence here: a 13/13-green autoscroll broke on a real trackpad, and the \"Show me how to fix this\" button passed every assertion while doing nothing"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 743,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`scripts/manual-check.sh` boots a seeded instance with both live (`--graft-ui` for the marketplace slot)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 744,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Judge, not assume:"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 745,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "top-fixed CSS toasts vs toast library"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 746,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`<details>` remedy vs modal"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 747,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "absolute vs live-relative timestamp"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 748,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "whole-panel swap vs patch"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 749,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "branding preview shows SAVED values, not as-you-type"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 750,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Branding colour pair now tested both directions \u2014 human check narrows to: swatch opens the OS dialog; picking a colour feels immediate"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 751,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Run it with someone who has not been building it"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "d26c25808ff6455c",
      "line_num": 740,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#frontend",
        "#ux"
      ],
      "text": "**Human UX review of the no-build surfaces: judge before any of them takes over a route (Alexander, 2026-07-28: \"it's close but the UX feels a little off\"). ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] `/admin/sprigs` vs `/pages/admin/sprigs` and `/admin/diagnostics` vs `/pages/admin/diagnostics` are both live \u2014 same data, same deployment \u2014 so judging is the cheapest it will ever be\n- [ ] A green suite is the WEAKEST evidence here: a 13/13-green autoscroll broke on a real trackpad, and the \"Show me how to fix this\" button passed every assertion while doing nothing\n- [ ] `scripts/manual-check.sh` boots a seeded instance with both live (`--graft-ui` for the marketplace slot)\n- [ ] Judge, not assume:\n- [ ] top-fixed CSS toasts vs toast library\n- [ ] `<details>` remedy vs modal\n- [ ] absolute vs live-relative timestamp\n- [ ] whole-panel swap vs patch\n- [ ] branding preview shows SAVED values, not as-you-type\n- [ ] Branding colour pair now tested both directions \u2014 human check narrows to: swatch opens the OS dialog; picking a colour feels immediate\n- [ ] Run it with someone who has not been building it\n\n`#frontend` `#ux`\n`TODO.md:L740`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 6180
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 753,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**SURVEYED: every migration candidate on one snapshot \u2014 the sorting key was wrong** (Alexander, 2026-08-02)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 754,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`cypress/e2e/upgrade/route-payload.cy.ts` 10/10 green on the restored snapshot (51 agents / 32 users / 17 knowledge bases / 8 prompts)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 755,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The floor: `/notes` with no data of its own costs 127 requests / 781 kB wire / 7,575 kB decoded"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 756,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Route deltas above it: prompts +121 kB, functions +206, users +296, knowledge +455, evaluations +1,269, agents +1,714, chat +5,170 \u2014 for six of eight routes the list is 2\u20136% of what loading it costs"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 757,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/api/models` is 2,304 kB, fetched on every route, never cached: 741 of the 781 kB wire (95%) on a warm client"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 758,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Server-rendered comparison: 12 requests / 234 kB wire / 472 kB decoded \u2014 one sixteenth of the EMPTY SvelteKit route"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 759,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Method: decoded kB is the ranking column; wire kB is a returning-visitor figure (cold numbers in `workshop-payload.cy.ts`); `/home` not surveyed \u2014 Spaces has no list hook yet"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 760,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend"
          ],
          "text": "**Reorder on lines deleted and open frequency \u2014 throughput no longer breaks ties.**"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 761,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Component lines: users 3,126 \u00b7 notes 2,910 \u00b7 knowledge 1,671 \u00b7 evaluations 1,359 \u00b7 functions 1,249 \u00b7 prompts 635 (ceilings \u2014 Agents landed at 53% of its count)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 762,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "No telemetry exists, so the frequency column stays empty until Alexander fills it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 763,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/admin/users` moves ahead of knowledge: largest component, the one surface that actually renders its base64 avatars, `users.cy.ts` already guards it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 764,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/notes` is judged off this table: 2,910 lines of editor, not a list \u2014 the props-and-forms pattern may not apply"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 765,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/workshop/prompts` as warm-up: 635 lines, +121 kB, an afternoon"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 766,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "_Floor part 1 of 3 done 2026-08-02: fonts and icons \u2212934 kB decoded on every SvelteKit route (spread 0.0 kB; floor 7,576.0 \u2192 6,642.5 kB, agents-legacy \u22121,056, server-rendered pages 0.0). Archivo 652 \u2192 187 kB, Vazirmatn 241 \u2192 111 kB plus a `unicode-range` so it loads only when Persian text is present; icon masters 512 \u2192 256 px at 45,710 bytes. First-visit win only \u2014 `/api/models` still never caches. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 767,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "_Two-sided `unicode-range` guard shipped (`cypress/e2e/font-unicode-range.cy.ts`): structural for too-wide (served stylesheet scopes the face to Arabic), behavioural for too-narrow (Persian text must pull the font), both proved able to fail; trap \u2014 the minifier rewrites `U+0600-06FF` as `U+6??`. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 768,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**THE FLOOR \u2014 parts 2 and 3: `/api/models` is the whole of what is left.**"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 769,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The floor stands at 6,642 kB; `/api/models` is 2,304 kB of it and never caches \u2014 741 kB over the wire on every navigation"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 770,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fixing the floor helps every route in the product, including the ones the strangler never reaches"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 771,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Stop fetching `/api/models` on routes that never render it \u2014 it rides the `(app)` layout boot wave (`+layout.svelte:120`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 772,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/notes`, `/admin/users`, `/admin/functions`, `/admin/evaluations` each pay 2.3 MB for a model list they never render"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 773,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Shrink the payload: `utils/models.py:175` sets `model[\"info\"] = custom_model.model_dump()` per row, base64 avatars included \u2014 why it is 2,304 kB instead of tens of kB"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 774,
          "tags": [
            "#backend"
          ],
          "text": "**`routers/knowledge.py:42` writes to the database during a GET and queries once per row.**"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 775,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`get_knowledge` calls `Files.get_file_metadatas_by_ids` per knowledge base (the `Models.get_models()` N+1 shape) and prunes dead file ids via `update_knowledge_data_by_id`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 776,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "So a concurrent read storm can write, and readers silently repair data"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 777,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fix AS the knowledge migration, on the \"prune, don't port\" rule"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 778,
          "tags": [
            "#backend",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**A prompt stored without a leading slash can never be fetched, edited or deleted \u2014 and every UI-imported prompt is stored that way** (found 2026-08-02 by the Prompts guard-rail)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 779,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Reproduced against a throwaway container; production snapshot unaffected \u2014 all 8 rows carry the slash"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 780,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`Prompts.insert_new_prompt` stores `command` verbatim while three readers look up `f\"/{command}\"` (`routers/prompts.py:99`, `:126`, `:161`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 781,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`Prompts.svelte`'s import handler strips the leading slash, so imported prompts are permanently undeletable and the UI shows no error"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 782,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Normalise at the write points \u2014 `insert_new_prompt` and `update_prompt_by_command` \u2014 not the three readers"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 783,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "One-line repair for existing rows lacking the slash"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 784,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The no-build panel must NOT port this: it normalises on lookup"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 785,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**Workshop is the next surface, elevated on production numbers** (Alexander, 2026-08-01)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 786,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Worst surface in the product; the only one missing the throughput budget (\u2264 ~2 MB transferred, first content < 2 s) on every axis"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 787,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/workshop/models` 144 requests / 20,520 kB / 6,181 kB transferred / 32 s"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 788,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/workshop/knowledge` ~140 requests / 18,203 kB / 5,257 kB / 19.07 s \u2014 a LIST OF MODELS slower than the 172 req / 7.9 MB / ~19 s conversation baseline"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 789,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "5,567 lines across models/knowledge/prompts; the table predicts ~50\u201365%"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 790,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "First task is a before-measurement \u2014 the last two such assumptions (22 MB WASM, markdown libs) measured false"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 791,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate, read not measured: serial waterfall \u2014 route awaits `getModels` before `<Models />`, which then fetches `getWorkshopModels` + `getGroups` + `getBranding`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 792,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate: static `marked`, `sortablejs`, `file-saver` in `Models.svelte`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 793,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate: static `fuse.js`, `dayjs` + `relativeTime` in `Knowledge.svelte`"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 794,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Candidate: base64 `model.meta.profile_image_url` per row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 795,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf",
            "#critical"
          ],
          "text": "**The list payload repeats the same owner avatar once per agent** (filed 2026-08-01, measured 2026-08-02; `cypress/e2e/upgrade/workshop-payload.cy.ts` on the snapshot)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 796,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`GET /api/v1/models/` nests the owner's whole `UserResponse` per row: 475 kB of base64 avatars the page never renders (rows show \"By {name}\" as text)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 797,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "21 of 32 users carry avatars, 120 kB amplified ~4\u00d7 by repetition"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 798,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`/api/models` 2,304 kB + `/api/v1/models/` 1,503 kB = 3,807 kB \u2014 41% of the page load, two endpoints carrying the same base64"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 799,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "SPA: 126 requests / 3,604 kB wire / 9,174 kB decoded / 5.4 s to first row; production's 20 MB does not fully reproduce (requests within 13%, bytes ~half)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 800,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Server-rendered: 11 requests / 234 kB / 152 ms cold, 7 kB / 44 ms repeat (0 data URIs vs 66; 6 cacheable avatar URLs)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 801,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "In-app arrival still costs 919 kB wire (914 kB is `/api/v1/models/`) and 1,504 ms to first row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 802,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Timing stamped in-browser with `performance.now()` at the click, because `Date.now()` in a Cypress body stamps at queue time"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 803,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Like-for-like (server page 1 is 24 rows vs the SPA's 51, so count both pages): 22 requests / ~477 kB \u2014 7.6\u00d7 less wire, 5.7\u00d7 fewer requests"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 804,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Also: `Models.get_models()` calls `Users.get_user_by_id()` in its loop \u2014 49 queries for 48 rows"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 805,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "_Parity gate earned its keep 2026-08-02: the Agents empty state dropped the `agents-list` container \u2014 invisible to every behavioural spec (`workshop-agents.cy.ts` seeds three agents first), visible to the gate that reads hooks. Fixed by one always-present container, `{% else %}` deleted; parity 8/8, Agents 9/9. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 806,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "_Startr Swap shipped 2026-08-09: links and forms swap in place via `pages/assets/startr-swap.js` (11,932 B raw / 5,343 gz vs htmx 50,917 / 16,367); `/settings/calendar` hollowed; suite 46 specs / 234 tests / 190 passing / 0 failing / 4m10s; `make startr_swap_check` runs in `gauntlet_full`; record `docs/decisions/2026-08-09-startr-swap-link-swapping.md`. OPEN: startr.style's licence conflict (LICENSE AGPL-3.0 / LICENSE.txt MIT / package.json ISC) blocks publishing, and nobody has reviewed any of it. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 807,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf"
          ],
          "text": "**A 166 kB favicon, a 166 kB splash and a 636 kB unsubsetted `Archivo-Variable.ttf` ride every cold page load** (found 2026-08-02 in the workshop top-25)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 808,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Reopens the line-395 `/icons/` \"not perf\" call, which judged the file on disk"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 809,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Just under 1 MB before anything renders, on the SPA and the server-rendered pages alike \u2014 PNG does not compress again on the wire, and a favicon is 16\u201348 px"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 810,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Cheap and separable from the migration: resize the icon set to the sizes actually declared"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 811,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Subset the font (line 105 already proposes automating the Cypress fixture copy)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 812,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf"
          ],
          "text": "~~**Agent avatars are uncompressed PNG data URIs inline in the list payload**~~ \u2014 REFUTED 2026-08-01 by the snapshot."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 813,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Only 16 of 324 `model` rows carry a data URI and all agent `meta` totals 868 kB \u2014 the third inference (after the 22 MB WASM and the markdown libs) that read perfectly and measured false"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 814,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Keep the cheap format fix as its own item: `toDataURL('image/webp', 0.8)` at slot-matched dimensions instead of default PNG at 250\u00d7250 (`ModelEditor.svelte:366`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 815,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#perf"
          ],
          "text": "**Avatars: one right size at the encoder plus a serve-time cache behind a cacheable URL \u2014 30\u00d7 measured, no new dependency beyond Pillow** (DECIDED 2026-08-01, Alexander)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 816,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Decision: migration AND serve-time cache, not encoder-only \u2014 the migration's job is getting the blob out of the database row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 817,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Three real 250\u00d7250 avatars: 106.8 / 97.7 / 95.0 kB as PNG, 21 kB as JPEG, 5.9\u20137.2 kB at 128 px, 3.6\u20134.5 kB at 88 px \u2014 format alone 5\u00d7, format-plus-size 30\u00d7"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 818,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Root cause: one canvas-resize block pasted three times (`ModelEditor.svelte:366`, `Settings/Account.svelte:134`, `ArenaModelModal.svelte:202`)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 819,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Only the agent copy omits the format argument, so it defaults to PNG"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 820,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "One shared encoder helper: WebP with JPEG fallback, dimensions matched to the slot"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 821,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Migration moves originals to content-addressed storage on the data volume, leaving a reference in the row"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 822,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Non-destructive (write, verify, then clear the row), idempotent, fails closed when the volume is not writable (`data_not_writable` issue_type)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 823,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Serve-time cache derives sizes beside the originals on first request; sizes come from a CLOSED set (44/128/256), never a free query parameter; cache on the volume, not in memory (multi-worker roadmap)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 824,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Exports must re-inline from storage and land WITH the migration \u2014 `Models.svelte:167` and `admin/Settings/Models.svelte:68` `JSON.stringify` models verbatim, so a local path silently breaks import portability"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 825,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Hardening: format allowlist, byte ceiling, `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS`; Pillow verified absent from `requirements.txt` and the built image"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 826,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Proof: `make upgrade_gate` boots a real snapshot"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 827,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend",
            "#brand"
          ],
          "text": "**Rename `/workshop/models` \u2192 `/workshop/agents`** (Alexander, 2026-08-01)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 828,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The UI already says Agents (`Models.svelte` heading, page title, Import/Export Agents); only the URL, directory and component names say models"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 829,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Consistent with the locked 2026-07-11 single tiered \"Agents\" surface decision"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 830,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Do it AS the migration \u2014 renaming twice costs two redirect layers"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 831,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The route, the nav label, the i18n keys, and a redirect from the old path for bookmarks"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 832,
          "tags": [
            "#biomes",
            "#ratchet"
          ],
          "text": "Count and pin the core biomes as a downward-only ratchet \u2014 chat core, rich-text editor, code editor, flow canvas, channels; the count only decreases"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 833,
          "tags": [
            "#frontend"
          ],
          "text": "**Mid-term: rebuild the chat core as an htmx flow, not a ported island** (Alexander, 2026-07-27)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 834,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The port is priced at 17,591 lines for a 15\u201330% cut"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 835,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "htmx-first has the server own the conversation and send fragments, only the token stream stays vanilla \u2014 Phase S proved that half in ~260 lines, abort semantics included"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 836,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A hypothesis with two Phase 0 datapoints; do NOT re-plan the phase order until one fragment surface is migrated and measured"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 837,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Phase 1 cookie bridge \u2014 fragments need the token off localStorage"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 838,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The non-proxying browser driver Phase S made a condition"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 839,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "One migrated, measured fragment surface \u2014 the datum that settles it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 840,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Reimplement the flow canvas (`@xyflow/svelte`) framework-free"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 841,
          "tags": [
            "#brand"
          ],
          "text": "Slogan precision: \"org-owned\" not \"user-owned\"; keep yjs local-first for the editor"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "e6af68723f14b4ec",
      "line_num": 752,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Phases 3\u20134 \u2014 medium surfaces, shell flip, then biomes: Workshop FIRST, then users, evals, settings tabs, chat list \u2192 prune biomes (Functions, then chat core last, gated on the spike memo). That order sorts on 2\u20136% of the cost (measured 2026-08-02) \u2014 reorder it. ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] **SURVEYED: every migration candidate on one snapshot \u2014 the sorting key was wrong** (Alexander, 2026-08-02). #frontend #perf #critical\n- [ ] `cypress/e2e/upgrade/route-payload.cy.ts` 10/10 green on the restored snapshot (51 agents / 32 users / 17 knowledge bases / 8 prompts)\n- [ ] The floor: `/notes` with no data of its own costs 127 requests / 781 kB wire / 7,575 kB decoded\n- [ ] Route deltas above it: prompts +121 kB, functions +206, users +296, knowledge +455, evaluations +1,269, agents +1,714, chat +5,170 \u2014 for six of eight routes the list is 2\u20136% of what loading it costs\n- [ ] `/api/models` is 2,304 kB, fetched on every route, never cached: 741 of the 781 kB wire (95%) on a warm client\n- [ ] Server-rendered comparison: 12 requests / 234 kB wire / 472 kB decoded \u2014 one sixteenth of the EMPTY SvelteKit route\n- [ ] Method: decoded kB is the ranking column; wire kB is a returning-visitor figure (cold numbers in `workshop-payload.cy.ts`); `/home` not surveyed \u2014 Spaces has no list hook yet\n- [ ] **Reorder on lines deleted and open frequency \u2014 throughput no longer breaks ties.** #frontend\n- [ ] Component lines: users 3,126 \u00b7 notes 2,910 \u00b7 knowledge 1,671 \u00b7 evaluations 1,359 \u00b7 functions 1,249 \u00b7 prompts 635 (ceilings \u2014 Agents landed at 53% of its count)\n- [ ] No telemetry exists, so the frequency column stays empty until Alexander fills it\n- [ ] `/admin/users` moves ahead of knowledge: largest component, the one surface that actually renders its base64 avatars, `users.cy.ts` already guards it\n- [ ] `/notes` is judged off this table: 2,910 lines of editor, not a list \u2014 the props-and-forms pattern may not apply\n- [ ] `/workshop/prompts` as warm-up: 635 lines, +121 kB, an afternoon\n- [x] _Floor part 1 of 3 done 2026-08-02: fonts and icons \u2212934 kB decoded on every SvelteKit route (spread 0.0 kB; floor 7,576.0 \u2192 6,642.5 kB, agents-legacy \u22121,056, server-rendered pages 0.0). Archivo 652 \u2192 187 kB, Vazirmatn 241 \u2192 111 kB plus a `unicode-range` so it loads only when Persian text is present; icon masters 512 \u2192 256 px at 45,710 bytes. First-visit win only \u2014 `/api/models` still never caches. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._\n- [x] _Two-sided `unicode-range` guard shipped (`cypress/e2e/font-unicode-range.cy.ts`): structural for too-wide (served stylesheet scopes the face to Arabic), behavioural for too-narrow (Persian text must pull the font), both proved able to fail; trap \u2014 the minifier rewrites `U+0600-06FF` as `U+6??`. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._\n- [ ] **THE FLOOR \u2014 parts 2 and 3: `/api/models` is the whole of what is left.** #frontend #perf #critical\n- [ ] The floor stands at 6,642 kB; `/api/models` is 2,304 kB of it and never caches \u2014 741 kB over the wire on every navigation\n- [ ] Fixing the floor helps every route in the product, including the ones the strangler never reaches\n- [ ] Stop fetching `/api/models` on routes that never render it \u2014 it rides the `(app)` layout boot wave (`+layout.svelte:120`)\n- [ ] `/notes`, `/admin/users`, `/admin/functions`, `/admin/evaluations` each pay 2.3 MB for a model list they never render\n- [ ] Shrink the payload: `utils/models.py:175` sets `model[\"info\"] = custom_model.model_dump()` per row, base64 avatars included \u2014 why it is 2,304 kB instead of tens of kB\n- [ ] **`routers/knowledge.py:42` writes to the database during a GET and queries once per row.** #backend\n- [ ] `get_knowledge` calls `Files.get_file_metadatas_by_ids` per knowledge base (the `Models.get_models()` N+1 shape) and prunes dead file ids via `update_knowledge_data_by_id`\n- [ ] So a concurrent read storm can write, and readers silently repair data\n- [ ] Fix AS the knowledge migration, on the \"prune, don't port\" rule\n- [ ] **A prompt stored without a leading slash can never be fetched, edited or deleted \u2014 and every UI-imported prompt is stored that way** (found 2026-08-02 by the Prompts guard-rail). #backend #critical\n- [ ] Reproduced against a throwaway container; production snapshot unaffected \u2014 all 8 rows carry the slash\n- [ ] `Prompts.insert_new_prompt` stores `command` verbatim while three readers look up `f\"/{command}\"` (`routers/prompts.py:99`, `:126`, `:161`)\n- [ ] `Prompts.svelte`'s import handler strips the leading slash, so imported prompts are permanently undeletable and the UI shows no error\n- [ ] Normalise at the write points \u2014 `insert_new_prompt` and `update_prompt_by_command` \u2014 not the three readers\n- [ ] One-line repair for existing rows lacking the slash\n- [ ] The no-build panel must NOT port this: it normalises on lookup\n- [ ] **Workshop is the next surface, elevated on production numbers** (Alexander, 2026-08-01). #frontend #perf #critical\n- [ ] Worst surface in the product; the only one missing the throughput budget (\u2264 ~2 MB transferred, first content < 2 s) on every axis\n- [ ] `/workshop/models` 144 requests / 20,520 kB / 6,181 kB transferred / 32 s\n- [ ] `/workshop/knowledge` ~140 requests / 18,203 kB / 5,257 kB / 19.07 s \u2014 a LIST OF MODELS slower than the 172 req / 7.9 MB / ~19 s conversation baseline\n- [ ] 5,567 lines across models/knowledge/prompts; the table predicts ~50\u201365%\n- [ ] First task is a before-measurement \u2014 the last two such assumptions (22 MB WASM, markdown libs) measured false\n- [ ] Candidate, read not measured: serial waterfall \u2014 route awaits `getModels` before `<Models />`, which then fetches `getWorkshopModels` + `getGroups` + `getBranding`\n- [ ] Candidate: static `marked`, `sortablejs`, `file-saver` in `Models.svelte`\n- [ ] Candidate: static `fuse.js`, `dayjs` + `relativeTime` in `Knowledge.svelte`\n- [ ] Candidate: base64 `model.meta.profile_image_url` per row\n- [ ] **The list payload repeats the same owner avatar once per agent** (filed 2026-08-01, measured 2026-08-02; `cypress/e2e/upgrade/workshop-payload.cy.ts` on the snapshot). #frontend #perf #critical\n- [ ] `GET /api/v1/models/` nests the owner's whole `UserResponse` per row: 475 kB of base64 avatars the page never renders (rows show \"By {name}\" as text)\n- [ ] 21 of 32 users carry avatars, 120 kB amplified ~4\u00d7 by repetition\n- [ ] `/api/models` 2,304 kB + `/api/v1/models/` 1,503 kB = 3,807 kB \u2014 41% of the page load, two endpoints carrying the same base64\n- [ ] SPA: 126 requests / 3,604 kB wire / 9,174 kB decoded / 5.4 s to first row; production's 20 MB does not fully reproduce (requests within 13%, bytes ~half)\n- [ ] Server-rendered: 11 requests / 234 kB / 152 ms cold, 7 kB / 44 ms repeat (0 data URIs vs 66; 6 cacheable avatar URLs)\n- [ ] In-app arrival still costs 919 kB wire (914 kB is `/api/v1/models/`) and 1,504 ms to first row\n- [ ] Timing stamped in-browser with `performance.now()` at the click, because `Date.now()` in a Cypress body stamps at queue time\n- [ ] Like-for-like (server page 1 is 24 rows vs the SPA's 51, so count both pages): 22 requests / ~477 kB \u2014 7.6\u00d7 less wire, 5.7\u00d7 fewer requests\n- [ ] Also: `Models.get_models()` calls `Users.get_user_by_id()` in its loop \u2014 49 queries for 48 rows\n- [x] _Parity gate earned its keep 2026-08-02: the Agents empty state dropped the `agents-list` container \u2014 invisible to every behavioural spec (`workshop-agents.cy.ts` seeds three agents first), visible to the gate that reads hooks. Fixed by one always-present container, `{% else %}` deleted; parity 8/8, Agents 9/9. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._\n- [x] _Startr Swap shipped 2026-08-09: links and forms swap in place via `pages/assets/startr-swap.js` (11,932 B raw / 5,343 gz vs htmx 50,917 / 16,367); `/settings/calendar` hollowed; suite 46 specs / 234 tests / 190 passing / 0 failing / 4m10s; `make startr_swap_check` runs in `gauntlet_full`; record `docs/decisions/2026-08-09-startr-swap-link-swapping.md`. OPEN: startr.style's licence conflict (LICENSE AGPL-3.0 / LICENSE.txt MIT / package.json ISC) blocks publishing, and nobody has reviewed any of it. Archived \u2192 docs/completed-todos.md._\n- [ ] **A 166 kB favicon, a 166 kB splash and a 636 kB unsubsetted `Archivo-Variable.ttf` ride every cold page load** (found 2026-08-02 in the workshop top-25). #frontend #perf\n- [ ] Reopens the line-395 `/icons/` \"not perf\" call, which judged the file on disk\n- [ ] Just under 1 MB before anything renders, on the SPA and the server-rendered pages alike \u2014 PNG does not compress again on the wire, and a favicon is 16\u201348 px\n- [ ] Cheap and separable from the migration: resize the icon set to the sizes actually declared\n- [ ] Subset the font (line 105 already proposes automating the Cypress fixture copy)\n- [ ] ~~**Agent avatars are uncompressed PNG data URIs inline in the list payload**~~ \u2014 REFUTED 2026-08-01 by the snapshot. #frontend #perf\n- [ ] Only 16 of 324 `model` rows carry a data URI and all agent `meta` totals 868 kB \u2014 the third inference (after the 22 MB WASM and the markdown libs) that read perfectly and measured false\n- [ ] Keep the cheap format fix as its own item: `toDataURL('image/webp', 0.8)` at slot-matched dimensions instead of default PNG at 250\u00d7250 (`ModelEditor.svelte:366`)\n- [ ] **Avatars: one right size at the encoder plus a serve-time cache behind a cacheable URL \u2014 30\u00d7 measured, no new dependency beyond Pillow** (DECIDED 2026-08-01, Alexander). #frontend #perf\n- [ ] Decision: migration AND serve-time cache, not encoder-only \u2014 the migration's job is getting the blob out of the database row\n- [ ] Three real 250\u00d7250 avatars: 106.8 / 97.7 / 95.0 kB as PNG, 21 kB as JPEG, 5.9\u20137.2 kB at 128 px, 3.6\u20134.5 kB at 88 px \u2014 format alone 5\u00d7, format-plus-size 30\u00d7\n- [ ] Root cause: one canvas-resize block pasted three times (`ModelEditor.svelte:366`, `Settings/Account.svelte:134`, `ArenaModelModal.svelte:202`)\n- [ ] Only the agent copy omits the format argument, so it defaults to PNG\n- [ ] One shared encoder helper: WebP with JPEG fallback, dimensions matched to the slot\n- [ ] Migration moves originals to content-addressed storage on the data volume, leaving a reference in the row\n- [ ] Non-destructive (write, verify, then clear the row), idempotent, fails closed when the volume is not writable (`data_not_writable` issue_type)\n- [ ] Serve-time cache derives sizes beside the originals on first request; sizes come from a CLOSED set (44/128/256), never a free query parameter; cache on the volume, not in memory (multi-worker roadmap)\n- [ ] Exports must re-inline from storage and land WITH the migration \u2014 `Models.svelte:167` and `admin/Settings/Models.svelte:68` `JSON.stringify` models verbatim, so a local path silently breaks import portability\n- [ ] Hardening: format allowlist, byte ceiling, `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS`; Pillow verified absent from `requirements.txt` and the built image\n- [ ] Proof: `make upgrade_gate` boots a real snapshot\n- [ ] **Rename `/workshop/models` \u2192 `/workshop/agents`** (Alexander, 2026-08-01). #frontend #brand\n- [ ] The UI already says Agents (`Models.svelte` heading, page title, Import/Export Agents); only the URL, directory and component names say models\n- [ ] Consistent with the locked 2026-07-11 single tiered \"Agents\" surface decision\n- [ ] Do it AS the migration \u2014 renaming twice costs two redirect layers\n- [ ] The route, the nav label, the i18n keys, and a redirect from the old path for bookmarks\n- [ ] Count and pin the core biomes as a downward-only ratchet \u2014 chat core, rich-text editor, code editor, flow canvas, channels; the count only decreases #biomes #ratchet\n- [ ] **Mid-term: rebuild the chat core as an htmx flow, not a ported island** (Alexander, 2026-07-27). #frontend\n- [ ] The port is priced at 17,591 lines for a 15\u201330% cut\n- [ ] htmx-first has the server own the conversation and send fragments, only the token stream stays vanilla \u2014 Phase S proved that half in ~260 lines, abort semantics included\n- [ ] A hypothesis with two Phase 0 datapoints; do NOT re-plan the phase order until one fragment surface is migrated and measured\n- [ ] Phase 1 cookie bridge \u2014 fragments need the token off localStorage\n- [ ] The non-proxying browser driver Phase S made a condition\n- [ ] One migrated, measured fragment surface \u2014 the datum that settles it\n- [ ] Reimplement the flow canvas (`@xyflow/svelte`) framework-free\n- [ ] Slogan precision: \"org-owned\" not \"user-owned\"; keep yjs local-first for the editor #brand\n\n`TODO.md:L752`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
