      "y": 780
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1139,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`SERVER_TAG` is the canonical server-image version read by the brew CLI, the Makefile fallback and the docs."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1140,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The tag still resolves correctly during a release because `GIT_TAG` outranks it in the precedence chain (`Makefile:74`) \u2014 the staleness is invisible until something reads the file directly."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1141,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The file has three hardlinks \u2014 source of truth `homebrew-apps/distribution.env`, mirrored into this repo and `WEB-Sage.Education-docs` \u2014 so it must be edited in place."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1142,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "macOS `sed -i` replaces the inode and breaks the chain."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1143,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Either teach `bump_release_version` to rewrite it inode-safely, or add it to the release runbook as an explicit manual step."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "0c756cfee29bf6ed",
      "line_num": 1138,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#release"
      ],
      "text": "**`bump_release_version` leaves `SERVER_TAG` on the previous release: the bump target updates only `app/package.json` and `README.md`, so `distribution.env` reads `SERVER_TAG=3.0.0` while 3.0.1 is being cut (found 2026-08-06 while readying 3.0.1).**\n- [ ] `SERVER_TAG` is the canonical server-image version read by the brew CLI, the Makefile fallback and the docs.\n- [ ] The tag still resolves correctly during a release because `GIT_TAG` outranks it in the precedence chain (`Makefile:74`) \u2014 the staleness is invisible until something reads the file directly.\n- [ ] The file has three hardlinks \u2014 source of truth `homebrew-apps/distribution.env`, mirrored into this repo and `WEB-Sage.Education-docs` \u2014 so it must be edited in place.\n- [ ] macOS `sed -i` replaces the inode and breaks the chain.\n- [ ] Either teach `bump_release_version` to rewrite it inode-safely, or add it to the release runbook as an explicit manual step.\n\n`#release`\n`TODO.md:L1138`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 870
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1145,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Mechanism: for a start tag not shaped `<...>`, `start_tag_pattern = re.escape(start_tag)` \u2014 zero capture groups \u2014 so when `\u25c1think\u25b7` appears in content, `re.search` matches and `match.group(1)` raises `IndexError`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1146,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The per-delta try swallows it, but the append already happened \u2014 EVERY later delta re-matches and re-raises BEFORE the emit and before the realtime save."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1147,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The reader sees a frozen message until the final done event delivers everything at once, with `\u25c1think\u25b7` rendered as text."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1148,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Kimi-family models emit exactly this tag."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1149,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The tuple is cannot-succeed code that also breaks live streaming \u2014 worse than dead."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1150,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "No net covers it; extending `reasoning-tag-fixture.py` with a `\u25c1think\u25b7` case is part of the fix."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1151,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Behaviour frozen until the structure work lands."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "a89bb760e7d3ba8f",
      "line_num": 1144,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**A literal `\u25c1think\u25b7` in streamed content freezes client-visible streaming for the rest of the stream: `tag_content_handler` keeps a zero-capture-group pattern, so `match.group(1)` raises `IndexError` on every later delta before the emit (found 2026-08-08 by the duplication sweep's dead-code lens, adversarially confirmed).**\n- [ ] Mechanism: for a start tag not shaped `<...>`, `start_tag_pattern = re.escape(start_tag)` \u2014 zero capture groups \u2014 so when `\u25c1think\u25b7` appears in content, `re.search` matches and `match.group(1)` raises `IndexError`.\n- [ ] The per-delta try swallows it, but the append already happened \u2014 EVERY later delta re-matches and re-raises BEFORE the emit and before the realtime save.\n- [ ] The reader sees a frozen message until the final done event delivers everything at once, with `\u25c1think\u25b7` rendered as text.\n- [ ] Kimi-family models emit exactly this tag.\n- [ ] The tuple is cannot-succeed code that also breaks live streaming \u2014 worse than dead.\n- [ ] No net covers it; extending `reasoning-tag-fixture.py` with a `\u25c1think\u25b7` case is part of the fix.\n- [ ] Behaviour frozen until the structure work lands.\n\n`#bug`\n`TODO.md:L1144`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 960
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1154,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Found while proving the title envelope cannot join the follow-ups/tags task runner."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1155,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A code comment now marks the emit site."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1156,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Frozen; fix belongs to [Unfreeze the ledger]."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "64fcd82f823a00f0",
      "line_num": 1153,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**The two-message title path persists one message and emits another: the `elif len(messages) == 2` arm persists `messages[0].get(\"content\", user_message)` \u2014 the FIRST \u2014 but emits `message.get(\"content\", user_message)` \u2014 the LAST \u2014 so the stored chat title and the one the reader watches arrive can differ (found 2026-08-08 by the sweep).**\n- [ ] Found while proving the title envelope cannot join the follow-ups/tags task runner.\n- [ ] A code comment now marks the emit site.\n- [ ] Frozen; fix belongs to [Unfreeze the ledger].\n\n`#bug`\n`TODO.md:L1153`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 1050
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1159,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Found 2026-08-08 during the chat-path weight census, while classifying it as dead code \u2014 it is not dead, it is a double-execution."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1160,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Continuation responses are spared \u2014 only `stream_body_handler` touches those."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1161,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Harmless if the background is an idempotent cleanup; not verified."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1162,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Deleting the second call is a behaviour change, so it is frozen with the rest."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "40ec9f194a2d88fd",
      "line_num": 1158,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**`response.background()` runs twice for the original streaming response: `stream_body_handler` awaits it at its tail for every response it drains; `response_handler` awaits it again on the same original after the retry loops \u2014 awaiting a Starlette `BackgroundTask` twice runs the wrapped callable twice.**\n- [ ] Found 2026-08-08 during the chat-path weight census, while classifying it as dead code \u2014 it is not dead, it is a double-execution.\n- [ ] Continuation responses are spared \u2014 only `stream_body_handler` touches those.\n- [ ] Harmless if the background is an idempotent cleanup; not verified.\n- [ ] Deleting the second call is a behaviour change, so it is frozen with the rest.\n\n`#bug`\n`TODO.md:L1158`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 1140
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1164,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Found 2026-08-08. Clean and fenced input parse; two objects in one reply do not."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1165,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "These calls run on the task model, which operators set small, and small models restate the format most."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1166,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Worst site is RAG queries ([middleware.py:1041](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1041)): on failure it sets the entire model reply as the retrieval query, silently degrading RAG."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1167,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(1) Set `response_format` on the task calls \u2014 `utils/payload.py:350-361` already converts it to Ollama's `format`, and no task call sets it. Behaviour: sequence after the structure work."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1168,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(2) One parser as the floor in a new `utils/llm_json.py` for providers that ignore it \u2014 strip fences, try the whole string, scan for balanced objects. New file, moves no citation; can land any time."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1169,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "(3) Drop the example object from the template. Behaviour: sequence after the structure work."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1170,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Trap: a shared helper is NOT the fix \u2014 in the restated-format case both objects are valid JSON and both carry the key, so no parser can tell them apart."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1171,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The six sites, consolidated 2026-08-08 into one `slice_json_object` helper, behaviour byte-identical:"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1172,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[797](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L797) tool calling"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1173,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[955](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L954) image prompt"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1174,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1042](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1041) RAG queries"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1175,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1498](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1499) follow-ups"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1176,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1543](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1543) title"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1177,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[1572](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1572) tags"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "921ad920d1018145",
      "line_num": 1163,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Six JSON parse sites scrape from the first `{` to the last `}`; the prompt template teaches the model to break it: `config.py:1584` ends the title template with a literal example object, so a model that restates the format emits two objects \u2014 exactly the input the scrape fails on. #bug ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] Found 2026-08-08. Clean and fenced input parse; two objects in one reply do not.\n- [ ] These calls run on the task model, which operators set small, and small models restate the format most.\n- [ ] Worst site is RAG queries ([middleware.py:1041](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1041)): on failure it sets the entire model reply as the retrieval query, silently degrading RAG.\n- [ ] (1) Set `response_format` on the task calls \u2014 `utils/payload.py:350-361` already converts it to Ollama's `format`, and no task call sets it. Behaviour: sequence after the structure work.\n- [ ] (2) One parser as the floor in a new `utils/llm_json.py` for providers that ignore it \u2014 strip fences, try the whole string, scan for balanced objects. New file, moves no citation; can land any time.\n- [ ] (3) Drop the example object from the template. Behaviour: sequence after the structure work.\n- [ ] Trap: a shared helper is NOT the fix \u2014 in the restated-format case both objects are valid JSON and both carry the key, so no parser can tell them apart.\n- [ ] The six sites, consolidated 2026-08-08 into one `slice_json_object` helper, behaviour byte-identical:\n- [ ] [797](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L797) tool calling\n- [ ] [955](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L954) image prompt\n- [ ] [1042](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1041) RAG queries\n- [ ] [1498](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1499) follow-ups\n- [ ] [1543](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1543) title\n- [ ] [1572](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1572) tags\n\n`TODO.md:L1163`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 1230
    },
