        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**A partial tag reaches the reader for one frame: when a chunk boundary splits a reasoning tag, the loop emits the fragment raw before the next chunk completes it \u2014 cosmetic and brief, but visible.**\n- [ ] The `reasoning-tag-inline` oracle golden records a first event whose entire content is `<thin`.\n- [ ] Same family as the chunk-boundary whitespace defect in the reasoning-tag entry below; a tag-aware output buffer would kill both at once.\n- [ ] Found 2026-08-04 while reading the oracle goldens (chat-path chart); logged not fixed \u2014 behaviour frozen, and the fix must re-record the golden deliberately.\n\n`#bug`\n`TODO.md:L1214`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 1770
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1220,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`supervisor.prune()` ([supervisor.py:1322](app/backend/sage_is_ai/sprigs/supervisor.py#L1322)) reverses no dispatch."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1221,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The router reset ([sprigs.py:275-300](app/backend/sage_is_ai/routers/sprigs.py#L275)) covers five `was_active_*` capabilities (embedding, reranker, stt, theme, ui) \u2014 tika and docling are absent."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1222,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`tika_dispatch.py:29` / `docling_dispatch.py:26` set the engine on graft; nothing unsets it (only other writers: `config.py:2117`, `main.py:1047`, `routers/retrieval.py:873`)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1223,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[boot.py:95-99](app/backend/sage_is_ai/diagnostics/boot.py#L95) probes `TIKA_SERVER_URL` whenever the engine is set; neither carries the `sprig-local` sentinel, so the `main.py` restart backstops miss it too."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1224,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Found 2026-08-05 (AIML responder charting); reported mechanically in the Gaps section of `docs/sprigs/capabilities.md`, gated by `make sprig_capabilities_check`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1225,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Quick fix: two more `was_active_*` resets beside the five in `sprigs.py`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1226,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Better: a `point_*_off(app, handle)` companion per dispatch module plus one registry read by the graft, boot-reconcile and prune fan-outs \u2014 today three hand-maintained copies of one table."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "c8303b387da9f7f8",
      "line_num": 1219,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bug",
        "#sprigs"
      ],
      "text": "**Pruning the Tika or Docling Sprig\u2122 leaves `CONTENT_EXTRACTION_ENGINE` aimed at a released port: `supervisor.prune()` reverses no dispatch and the router reset skips tika/docling \u2014 worst case a pruned tika permanently re-creates the \"unreachable\" alarm a previous fix killed. ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] `supervisor.prune()` ([supervisor.py:1322](app/backend/sage_is_ai/sprigs/supervisor.py#L1322)) reverses no dispatch.\n- [ ] The router reset ([sprigs.py:275-300](app/backend/sage_is_ai/routers/sprigs.py#L275)) covers five `was_active_*` capabilities (embedding, reranker, stt, theme, ui) \u2014 tika and docling are absent.\n- [ ] `tika_dispatch.py:29` / `docling_dispatch.py:26` set the engine on graft; nothing unsets it (only other writers: `config.py:2117`, `main.py:1047`, `routers/retrieval.py:873`).\n- [ ] [boot.py:95-99](app/backend/sage_is_ai/diagnostics/boot.py#L95) probes `TIKA_SERVER_URL` whenever the engine is set; neither carries the `sprig-local` sentinel, so the `main.py` restart backstops miss it too.\n- [ ] Found 2026-08-05 (AIML responder charting); reported mechanically in the Gaps section of `docs/sprigs/capabilities.md`, gated by `make sprig_capabilities_check`.\n- [ ] Quick fix: two more `was_active_*` resets beside the five in `sprigs.py`.\n- [ ] Better: a `point_*_off(app, handle)` companion per dispatch module plus one registry read by the graft, boot-reconcile and prune fan-outs \u2014 today three hand-maintained copies of one table.\n\n`#bug` `#sprigs`\n`TODO.md:L1219`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 1860
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "580c14e440d79a5d",
      "line_num": 1227,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#tests",
        "#bug"
      ],
      "text": "**~~`models-cache.cy.ts` gates a timing quantity, and it now fails on `HEAD`~~ (2026-08-04, superseded by the entry above \u2014 kept for the record of how the wrong answer looked right) ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n`#tests` `#bug`\n`TODO.md:L1227`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 1950
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1232,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`tag_content_handler` ([middleware.py:380](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L380)) closes only on its opening pair's exact end tag, with no end-of-stream finalizer."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1233,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The field-path close is guarded on `if value:` ([middleware.py:1850](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1850))."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1234,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Variant 1, tag drift: any open/close mismatch leaves the block open forever."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1235,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`scripts/smoke/reasoning-tag-fixture.py` fails 16 cases across 5 defects (`<thinking>` closed `</think>`, the reverse, `</THINKING>`, `</ thinking>`, never-closes)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1236,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "A sixth cosmetic case (space eaten at chunk=7, not chunk=1 or 999) explains the reported \"not always\"."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1237,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Variant 2, field path \u2014 the priority, reproduced from Alexander's capture: the literal `</thinking>` plus the whole answer stay sealed, `done=\"false\"`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1238,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "DeepSeek R1 templates pre-fill the opener into the PROMPT; a provider that streams everything through `reasoning` and sends no `content` delta never fires the `if value:` close."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1239,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Confirmed 3 ways 2026-08-04 on live code: chat `171f30b9`, 08:34 UTC, production snapshot on `:8102`; a `deepseek-r1-distill-llama-70b` call with 736 reasoning chars and 0 content; a control that closed."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1240,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Trigger: a UI-built agent whose system prompt asks for `<thinking>` tags on a native-reasoning provider."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1241,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Variant 3 (2026-08-06, `qwen3.5:9b` via Ollama, chat `aafdddab`): a bare `</think>` with no opener arrives in the CONTENT stream and renders as text."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1242,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "The field path opens AND closes correctly (`done=\"true\"`) first; the field path opens it, the tag path orphans the close."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1243,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Not a regression: pre- and post-tightening replays were byte-identical."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1244,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fix (1): end-of-stream finalizer \u2014 close any reasoning block still open when the stream ends and surface its content."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1245,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fix (2): treat an unpaired closing tag as an implicit opening at position zero (tag-path variant)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1246,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Does NOT cover variant 3 \u2014 there, DROP an orphan close tag when a reasoning block already closed in the same message."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1247,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Fix (3): widen the close match to any end tag in the list, case-insensitive, `</\\s*tag\\s*>`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1248,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Remove the `<<thinking>(.*?)>` start-tag strip WITH a fixture case \u2014 it eats literal `<<thinking>\u2026>` spans, silently deleting reasoning content."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1249,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "NOT dead (proven 2026-08-08 after a session deleted and restored it)."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1250,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Extend the fixture to the field path before trusting it; today it mirrors the TAG path only."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1251,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "READ FIRST: golden `fixtures/chat-response/reasoning-field-closed-then-orphan.sse` (oracle replays 12 streams) FREEZES the variant-3 leak as it is; read it before changing the tag logic."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1252,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Its job is to go RED when fix (2) lands \u2014 an implicit open there would mint a second block and swallow the answer."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 1253,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Line numbers restated 2026-08-04 (stale by ~93 before the \u2212160 dead-handler deletion); re-derive from the quoted source text, not the number."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "fcaef8b3c0c74b4e",
      "line_num": 1231,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Unclosed reasoning block swallows the model's answer (Alexander, 2026-08-03; demo-blocking): no close path has an end-of-stream finalizer \u2014 worst case the whole answer stays sealed inside the collapsed reasoning block, or private reasoning renders as text. Three variants. #critical #bug ([dossier](docs/board-dossiers.md))**\n- [ ] `tag_content_handler` ([middleware.py:380](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L380)) closes only on its opening pair's exact end tag, with no end-of-stream finalizer.\n- [ ] The field-path close is guarded on `if value:` ([middleware.py:1850](app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L1850)).\n- [ ] Variant 1, tag drift: any open/close mismatch leaves the block open forever.\n- [ ] `scripts/smoke/reasoning-tag-fixture.py` fails 16 cases across 5 defects (`<thinking>` closed `</think>`, the reverse, `</THINKING>`, `</ thinking>`, never-closes).\n- [ ] A sixth cosmetic case (space eaten at chunk=7, not chunk=1 or 999) explains the reported \"not always\".\n- [ ] Variant 2, field path \u2014 the priority, reproduced from Alexander's capture: the literal `</thinking>` plus the whole answer stay sealed, `done=\"false\"`.\n- [ ] DeepSeek R1 templates pre-fill the opener into the PROMPT; a provider that streams everything through `reasoning` and sends no `content` delta never fires the `if value:` close.\n- [ ] Confirmed 3 ways 2026-08-04 on live code: chat `171f30b9`, 08:34 UTC, production snapshot on `:8102`; a `deepseek-r1-distill-llama-70b` call with 736 reasoning chars and 0 content; a control that closed.\n- [ ] Trigger: a UI-built agent whose system prompt asks for `<thinking>` tags on a native-reasoning provider.\n- [ ] Variant 3 (2026-08-06, `qwen3.5:9b` via Ollama, chat `aafdddab`): a bare `</think>` with no opener arrives in the CONTENT stream and renders as text.\n- [ ] The field path opens AND closes correctly (`done=\"true\"`) first; the field path opens it, the tag path orphans the close.\n- [ ] Not a regression: pre- and post-tightening replays were byte-identical.\n- [ ] Fix (1): end-of-stream finalizer \u2014 close any reasoning block still open when the stream ends and surface its content.\n- [ ] Fix (2): treat an unpaired closing tag as an implicit opening at position zero (tag-path variant).\n- [ ] Does NOT cover variant 3 \u2014 there, DROP an orphan close tag when a reasoning block already closed in the same message.\n- [ ] Fix (3): widen the close match to any end tag in the list, case-insensitive, `</\\s*tag\\s*>`.\n- [ ] Remove the `<<thinking>(.*?)>` start-tag strip WITH a fixture case \u2014 it eats literal `<<thinking>\u2026>` spans, silently deleting reasoning content.\n- [ ] NOT dead (proven 2026-08-08 after a session deleted and restored it).\n- [ ] Extend the fixture to the field path before trusting it; today it mirrors the TAG path only.\n- [ ] READ FIRST: golden `fixtures/chat-response/reasoning-field-closed-then-orphan.sse` (oracle replays 12 streams) FREEZES the variant-3 leak as it is; read it before changing the tag logic.\n- [ ] Its job is to go RED when fix (2) lands \u2014 an implicit open there would mint a second block and swallow the answer.\n- [ ] Line numbers restated 2026-08-04 (stale by ~93 before the \u2212160 dead-handler deletion); re-derive from the quoted source text, not the number.\n\n`TODO.md:L1231`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1060,
      "y": 2040
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
