    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "e811a4a76adf351b",
      "line_num": 169,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**A home page that carries the widget: `/pages/home` is built on the no-build stack, open to every signed-in reader, carrying the slot by construction. The Svelte `/home` gained the same hooks, the surface is registered, and the parity sets match in both data states. Still owed: a container run with a grafted fragment, and a human pass \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-08-central-intelligence-home-page.md)**\n`charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md:L169`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1320
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "5677a05c4d770bee",
      "line_num": 171,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Five rows by hand: six fields survived \u2014 who, stage, threads, owed, empty pans, links. Owed works as a table, and stage needs a second line saying what moves it. The record's first act was to expose a hole: nobody wrote down what happened at Realtor R's kickoff on 2026-08-07. Two findings became cards, and `.clients.md:19` turns out to be damaged \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-08-central-intelligence-row-shape.md)**\n`charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md:L171`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1410
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "7557c4ccdf9f1acf",
      "line_num": 173,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**What a Resident Agent\u2122 gives us: the repo went public and we read it. The Sage.is integration already works, over an OpenAI-compatible API with SSE streaming. Projects are the vault \u2014 a directory per project with approved-directory boundaries. Two harnesses run, Claude Code and OpenCode. A scheduler and a webhook receiver already ship. It runs on a Pi 4 \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-08-central-intelligence-resident-agent.md)**\n`charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md:L173`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1500
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "335f8daf8326eb11",
      "line_num": 175,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Where a widget mounts: `#sprig-ui-slot` renders server-side on `/pages` surfaces only, and `/home` is Svelte, so the widget cannot reach it today. Two limits shape everything downstream: the slot revalidates on every render, and only one ui-Sprig can be active per instance \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-08-central-intelligence-widget-mount.md)**\n`charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md:L175`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1590
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "b5d927b2487af1ce",
      "line_num": 177,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**What the Telegram toggle exposes: it ships, it defaults off, and flipping it connects nothing. The toggle only reveals a BotFather token field plus a warning that messages reach this agent over Telegram. Two deliberate acts, because fetching a token is the errand that makes the accident impossible. An allowlist is proposed as the third wire \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-08-central-intelligence-telegram-toggle.md)**\n`charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md:L177`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1680
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "4edad9358e88ea73",
      "line_num": 179,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Can an agent write the record: a Base Agent cannot, and not by writing code. Base Agents read knowledge through retrieval, and every tool they call is an admin-configured OpenAPI tool server. A Resident Agent\u2122 writes files directly and needs no shim \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-08-central-intelligence-agent-write-path.md)**\n`charts/central-intelligence/TODO.md:L179`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 1770
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/aiml-responder/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "58b0a220f3d1810b",
      "line_num": 148,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
