      "text": "**The raw tool-call hole, closed (2026-08-08, evening \u2014 the first behaviour fix after [Re-tighten and re-point], elevated by Alexander to \"deal with soon\"): `_render_tool_calls_raw` emits Hermes-style `<tool_call>`/`<tool_response>` tags, so the code-interpreter continuation at [middleware.py:2172](../../app/backend/sage_is_ai/utils/middleware.py#L2172) hands the model its complete tool round instead of a hole. Golden re-recorded with exactly 10 changed outputs, all `raw=True` tool-call cases; oracle 12/12 byte-identical; both ratchets held (the first draft tripped BOTH \u2014 a 4th `except: pass` and cognitive 18 on new code \u2014 and was restructured rather than granted a ceiling). The sitting also caught systematic citation rot the gate cannot see: bare-number labels missing every re-point pass, plus seven anchors carrying dead mid-campaign coordinates (`process_chat_response` cited at 1439 while its def sat at 1420); all now content-verified. middleware 2,227 \u2192 2,271 lines, and worth it \u2014**\n`charts/chat-path-restructure/TODO.md:L268`",
