      "line_num": 123,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Social preview: accepted 2026-08-03 \u2014 Alexander reviewed the rendered card and the copy (_\"We're good with the art and copy. We looked.\"_). Ships with 3.1.0 as a rough card, knowingly not final art. Mark and type were enlarged before acceptance and judged at 500px, the width a feed renders at. Mechanism verified: 11 og tags, `og:image` 200 `image/jpeg`, declared dimensions matching the file, block omitted whole when `WEBUI_URL` is unset, and the accepted bytes confirmed inside the built image rather than only on disk \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-03-social-preview-accepted.md)**\n`charts/friday-demo/TODO.md:L123`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 3300
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/friday-demo/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "d3432832833048bd",
      "line_num": 125,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**The version jump \u2014 REOPENED 2026-08-09, it was ticked and it did not happen: `git tag --list` ends at `v3.0.0` and `git ls-remote --tags origin` agrees; live `/api/config` returns 3.0.0 and the served `index.html` carries `Last-Modified: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:25:32 GMT`. Two independent tells confirm the build: `/static/icons/favicon.svg` still answers 200 with 202,944 bytes (develop deleted that file on 2026-08-03), and the served `<head>` still has the `image/svg+xml` link develop removed. The instance is 99 commits behind develop, not the 71 recorded below. The tick recorded a DECISION, not a release. DECIDED 2026-08-09 by Alexander: cut it and deploy. _\"there's no reason we can't deploy our changes. Everything has been working. We have live Pullbots\"_ \u2014 and the evidence backs him: full suite 234 tests, 190 passing, 0 failing, `sprig_smoke` 68/0, `scan_tree` clean. The earlier caution here was about the SIZE of the change (99 commits, 375 files, 24 days, no staging) rather than about any observed breakage, and size is not evidence. Two conditions carry over because they are about the registry, not the code: pin the deploy to `@sha256:<index-digest>`, and verify the RUNNING image rather than the built one \u2014 CapRover served a stale image on this instance once already. Verify with a POSITIVE signal, not the absence of the old favicon: `GET /pages/home` must return a real server-rendered page containing `data-cy=\"page-heading\"`, and `GET /pages/_assets/startr-swap.js` must return 200. Both are things only develop serves; both are 0 files at `v3.0.0`. An absence-based check reads as a defect and cannot tell a new image from a broken one. Original card text follows. cut 3.1.0 off develop through the normal git-flow release and run Monday on it; 3.0.1 and an untagged develop deploy both rejected. Anonymous `/` flips to the server-rendered welcome page by itself when it boots, which is where the social tags go and where Reviewer T's fix lands. Riding the release: OG tags on the server-rendered pages only, a new share image, `web-app-manifest-512x512.png` (170,761 B), `favicon.svg` (202,944 B). The cut line is dissolved \u2014 a tag off develop ships every surface, so the question collapsed into [Tour route list] \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-03-version-jump-to-3.1.0.md)**\n`charts/friday-demo/TODO.md:L125`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 3390
    },
    {
      "file_path": "charts/friday-demo/TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "2ca76cfbfb837d77",
      "line_num": 127,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**Screen inventory: read live 2026-08-03. The instance runs v3.0.0 and is 71 commits behind develop, so no server-rendered surface is live and Reviewer T's mobile fix is not deployed; four of five agents answer `Model not found`; the School B residue is three empty knowledge bases and 15.1 kB of stored content in total; `/api/models` is 11.9 kB here rather than the board's 2,304 kB \u2014 [decision](../../docs/decisions/2026-08-03-try-sage-screen-inventory.md)**\n`charts/friday-demo/TODO.md:L127`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 3480
    }
